    },
    "l10n.readme.pixel-font-coverage" : {
      "comment" : "R9 / iteration 7. THE CATALOG HEADER, and the one thing to read before adding a language.\n\nThis catalog is extracted from source by the build (SWIFT_EMIT_LOC_STRINGS=YES, LOCALIZATION_PREFERS_STRING_CATALOGS=YES); do not hand-edit the extracted entries.\n\nPIXEL TEXT IS ENGLISH-AND-DOLLARS ONLY. PixelText draws through PixelFont, a 5x7 bitmap face with exactly 55 glyphs: A-Z (26), 0-9 (10), space, and $ . , : - + / ! ? ' % ( ) and the five symbols  x  .  >  heart  star  (19 non-alphanumerics in all). No lowercase (input is uppercased), no accented letters, no currency but the dollar, no & # @ quotes or brackets. Anything outside the table draws a hollow box (PixelChromeTests pins that). A German or French string routed through PixelText would render as boxes, so a second language needs the Latin-1 extension (~60 glyphs) first -- wave 2.\n\nNUMBERS STAY EN_US_POSIX. Theme.gameLocale pins every in-game figure to en_US_POSIX and MoneySnapshotTests guards it, because a locale's grouping separator (a space, a non-breaking space, an apostrophe) can be a character the face cannot draw. Money is the game's currency, not the player's. Do not localize it with the UI.\n\nSENTENCES ARE NOT HERE YET. EventCopy, NewspaperComposer, PostMortem and FounderBiographyView build sentences by concatenation; each site carries a '// l10n:' comment naming the format string it would become. Converting them is its own lane.\n\nCONTENT JSON IS NOT HERE EITHER. Events.json, LifeEvents.json, StaffEvents.json, News.json, Reviews.json, Dialogue.json and Goals.json stay as they are; the path is ContentCatalog.load(locale:) reading Resources/<lang>.lproj/<file>.json overlays keyed by id with per-string English fallback -- wave 2, and engine-neutral because ids never change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Startup Studio"
          }
        }
      }
